From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Jul 2026 02:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clocksource: sky1: defer probe on missing timer clocks, preserve real error

Confirmed live on Orion O6N 2026-07-19/20: sky1_timer_probe() hard-
returns -EINVAL when either clock lookup fails, discarding the real
error entirely -- even if devm_clk_get() already returned the
retryable -EPROBE_DEFER, this code throws it away and substitutes a
fixed -EINVAL, which the driver core never retries. Combined with
the driver's own "initialized" static guard (probe only ever
attempted meaningfully once), a clock not yet mapped by clk-sky1-acpi
at first probe permanently disables this SoC's system timer for the
rest of boot -- more consequential than the peripheral-driver
instances of this same bug class (0162-0165/2021-2024) since this is
the clocksource, not an optional peripheral.

Same -ENOENT-to-EPROBE_DEFER translation as those fixes, plus
propagating the real PTR_ERR via dev_err_probe() instead of a fixed
-EINVAL.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/clocksource/timer-sky1-gpt.c b/drivers/clocksource/timer-sky1-gpt.c
index 15fc234..04a0418 100644
--- a/drivers/clocksource/timer-sky1-gpt.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/timer-sky1-gpt.c
@@ -324,11 +324,17 @@ static int sky1_timer_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	sky1tm->pclk = devm_clk_get(&pdev->dev, "fch_timer_apb_clk");
 	if (IS_ERR(sky1tm->pclk))
-		return -EINVAL;
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev,
+				     PTR_ERR(sky1tm->pclk) == -ENOENT ?
+				     -EPROBE_DEFER : PTR_ERR(sky1tm->pclk),
+				     "failed to get fch_timer_apb_clk\n");
 
 	sky1tm->tclk = devm_clk_get(&pdev->dev, "fch_timer_func_clk");
 	if (IS_ERR(sky1tm->tclk))
-		return -EINVAL;
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev,
+				     PTR_ERR(sky1tm->tclk) == -ENOENT ?
+				     -EPROBE_DEFER : PTR_ERR(sky1tm->tclk),
+				     "failed to get fch_timer_func_clk\n");
 
 	clk_prepare_enable(sky1tm->pclk);
 	clk_prepare_enable(sky1tm->tclk);
--
